# Static analysis for this project's C sources (the detekt / Android lint
# equivalent). Run: tools/lint.sh
#
# Enabled: bug-pattern checks (bugprone), the clang static analyzer, misc and
# performance. Disabled below, with the reason, are checks that only produce
# noise for this codebase.
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-assignment-in-if-condition,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.strcpy,
  cert-err34-c,
  misc-*,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-unused-parameters,
  -misc-header-include-cycle,
  performance-*,
  readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  readability-isolate-declaration,
  readability-duplicate-include,
  readability-misleading-indentation,
  readability-redundant-*,
  readability-else-after-return
# Why the exclusions:
# - easily-swappable-parameters: flags every (int, int) function
# - assignment-in-if-condition: `if ((err = f()) != ESP_OK)` is idiomatic here
# - insecureAPI.*: wants C11 Annex K (memcpy_s, snprintf_s), which newlib
#   doesn't have; snprintf/memcpy with sizeof() are the norm
# - include-cleaner: ESP-IDF headers are umbrella headers by design
# - unused-parameters: ESP-IDF callback signatures are fixed
# - header-include-cycle: fires inside ESP-IDF's own FreeRTOS headers
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*/main/.*'
CheckOptions:
  readability-function-cognitive-complexity.Threshold: 40
  # ESP_LOGx / ESP_ERROR_CHECK expand to branches: counting them makes
  # every function with logging look complex.
  readability-function-cognitive-complexity.IgnoreMacros: true
